From 4c24cf8fad13aa8332798c01462bcc5f6f587944 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: tomaszstaniak <nbw.designs@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 2 Sep 2026 11:16:48 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 2/2] runtime: route GOOS=aros onto the Plan 9-shaped build
 tags

Registers aros/amd64 as a platform and regenerates internal/goos, then
picks the shared implementations that fit a system with no mmap, no
futex, no Unix signal delivery and no poller: mem_sbrk, lock_sema,
netpoll_stub, and our own time and low-level stubs.

Keeps the generated allocator tables rather than Plan 9's empty ones --
that substitution is a space saving we do not need.

Cuts the undefined OS-layer symbols from 57 to 37. Nothing runs yet.
